  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2227$,\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2228.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is negative **or** rational. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{\u00a0is negative\u00a0}}_{\u23df}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{x\\text{\u00a0is rational\u00a0}}_{\u23df}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N\u2228R.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is positive **or** an integer. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{\u00a0is positive\u00a0}}_{\u23df}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{x\\text{\u00a0is an integer\u00a0}}_{\u23df}}_{I},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P\u2228I.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{\u00a0is negative or rational}}_{\u23df}}_{N\\,\u2228\\,R}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2227}\\,{{x\\text{\u00a0is positive or an integer\u00a0}}_{\u23df}}_{P\\,\u2228\\,I},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(N\u2228R)\u2227(P\u2228I).$",
